id: pm-vcs-provenance-catalog-scale
title: Measure and compact native provenance catalogs without weakening recovery
description: "Follow-up to PR 150 native erasure provenance. The correctness repair records one identity-only payload ownership file per object/FileId edge and rewrites the current native-output registry when publishing a working file. Measure complete data-plus-control byte, inode and write costs across growing histories and materialized working sets. Evaluate a compact catalog or batch publication only with equivalent durable source attribution before bytes, strict native ownership classification, backward-readable schemas and every crash/recovery guard retained. Existing object-root pack measurements do not establish total clone metadata or checkout scaling."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: follow-up,performance,provenance
created_at: "2026-11-01T02:12:37.718Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T08:58:25.501Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Publish data-plus-control byte and inode counts and write/read costs for increasing FileId histories; preserve native source closure, refusal schemas, publication ordering and crash convergence; keep existing coverage thresholds and backward reads; make no performance claim before measurement."
parent: pm-vcs-phase6packs
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-01T08:27:31.274Z",codex-agent,"Sixth-review triage adds PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6yWzbL (per-file outputs registry rewrites/fsync cost) and PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6yWzcn (per-node denial-stamp syscalls). These are valid scale optimization work within this already accepted separate follow-up, not weakened correctness barriers. Publishing one registry only after checkout bytes would lose interrupted-output provenance; caching denials requires a live lease/policy-generation proof. Measure and amortize these costs while preserving birth-before-bytes and revocation checks."
  "2026-11-01T08:58:25.501Z",codex-agent,"Cubic threads PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6yWzbL and PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6yWzcn remain in this existing scale follow-up: native-output writes must remain intent-before-bytes, so batching cannot simply publish the registry after checkout. Denial caches must retain generation/lease fences. The new 150000-entry real-tree queue regression also measures a pre-existing quadratic duplicate-name decoder, which is separate from the repaired argument-spread overflow; preserve duplicate-name validation when optimizing it."
